WEBVTT

00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:05.547
Heavy metal exposure can lead to damage
to cell components due to their chemistry.

00:00:05.755 --> 00:00:08.591
These metals can engage
in a range of redox

00:00:08.591 --> 00:00:12.846
reactions that create reactive oxygen
species and induce

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:16.891
oxidative stress,
leading to damage to macromolecules

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:21.021
including lipids, proteins,
and nucleic acids.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:24.607
Damage to lipids affects cell membranes,

00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:28.903
a structure critical for cell integrity
and both a barrier

00:00:28.903 --> 00:00:33.491
and facilitator of movement of materials
in and out of the cell.

00:00:34.117 --> 00:00:37.662
Proteins are involved
in numerous functions in the cells

00:00:37.996 --> 00:00:40.957
and damage interferes
with protein activity,

00:00:40.999 --> 00:00:44.711
including inhibition of enzymes,
inactivation

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:48.381
of proteins,
and change of protein shape and function.

00:00:49.007 --> 00:00:52.844
DNA damage can lead to cell death
by apoptosis

00:00:52.844 --> 00:00:57.432
or DNA repair, but improper
DNA repair can lead to cancer.
